WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.923 --> 00:00:03.996
- There's something quite
primal about being in a tree,

00:00:03.996 --> 00:00:07.163
something that just feels really safe.

00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:10.626
It's just great.

00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:12.318
Go climb a tree.

00:00:12.318 --> 00:00:15.151
(acoustic guitar)

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:20.891
An arborist is somebody who
takes care of the trees.

00:00:20.891 --> 00:00:25.185
We prune, maintain, and
remove if dangerous.

00:00:25.185 --> 00:00:28.057
Really the whole healthcare of a tree.

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:30.588
In Melbourne, we're quite
lucky in the ranges.

00:00:30.588 --> 00:00:33.376
There's trees up there
that are 85, 90 meters.

00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:35.459
Really, really big trees.

00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:39.075
At the moment, I'm about 24,

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.737
22, 24 meters up a tree,

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:44.644
in a beautiful old red gum.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.928
This old tree we're in today
is maybe 250 years old,

00:00:47.928 --> 00:00:51.097
and it would be such a
shame to the landscape

00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:53.430
to lose something like this.

00:00:56.705 --> 00:00:58.498
Is it dangerous?

00:00:58.498 --> 00:01:00.381
It probably, yeah, it
must be really dangerous.

00:01:00.381 --> 00:01:01.998
I mean it's one of the most
dangerous jobs in the world,

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:02.915
apparently.

00:01:05.366 --> 00:01:07.382
Every single tree has something different

00:01:07.382 --> 00:01:09.799
that you have to put into it.

00:01:15.066 --> 00:01:18.707
That hole is just big enough
to take one of the syringes

00:01:18.707 --> 00:01:20.665
and actually prevent all these leaf-miners

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:22.225
from attacking those leaves.

00:01:22.225 --> 00:01:24.964
Working with trees and understanding trees

00:01:24.964 --> 00:01:26.467
and having a respect for trees

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:30.634
is the only way I think you
can really then cut the trees.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.230
The thing is, sometimes a
tree needs to come down.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.568
If there's an obvious failure,
or disease or something,

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:46.177
then we're the best ones to
come out, remove it safely,

00:01:46.177 --> 00:01:49.202
and advise about how we can replant.

00:01:49.202 --> 00:01:50.693
We're here actually trying to preserve

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:51.661
and look after the trees,

00:01:51.661 --> 00:01:55.661
because we very much have
an affection for them.

00:01:57.385 --> 00:02:00.218
(acoustic guitar)

